      "writtenOn": "2026-09-17T04:46:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The function returns a `std::string`, which is explicitly `dynamic`. Per C++ Core Guideline F.20, `A return value is self-documenting...` Since the function clearly communicates that it returns `dynamic-length data`, the caller is entirely responsible for bounds-checking if they decide to `force` that data into a `fixed-length` container like a `std::u32string`.\n\nhttps://isocpp.github.io/CppCoreGuidelines/CppCoreGuidelines#f20-for-out-output-values-prefer-return-values-to-output-parameters",
